    "description": "Family of digital indicating devices designated DD1010, DD1010I, DD1010IC, DD1010H, DD1010IH and DD1010ICH (each also available with the alternative 'Flynet' motherboard, designation suffixed 'Flynet') connected to a weighing platform to form a Class III or IIII, AC mains or DC-powered, self-indicating, non-automatic weighing instrument. The instruments shall not be used for direct sales to the public. Devices: initial zero setting, semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, automatic zero setting (negative load indications for more than 5 s), semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, preset tare, MPP Alibi storage device, up to 2 load receptors with summation, weighbridge modes (AdR/RDA, RcD, RpD/RCP), identification and recognition of A/D converters, digital load cells and DILINK junction box, encrypted weight data transmission to a remote indicator (load receptor and indicator must be simultaneously visible), optional connection to an external PC. Interfaces (max 30 m): load cell 6-wire shielded connection (analogue/digital), TTL 5V (not fitted with analogue load cell connection), RS232/422/485, Ethernet, Wi-Fi on core module (internal antenna), 0-10 V / 0-20 mA analogue input/output, digital I/O, field bus (Profibus...), USB host, SD card, audio; Flynet models additionally offer HDMI in place of TTL 5V. Sealing: physical sealing measures, common serial numbers, wire-and-seal, or software solution using recognition of unique S/N; SD card access prevented by tamper-evident seal; calibration/metrological configuration protected via physically protected switch or password with non-resettable 'SW seal counter'."
